{"id":411,"name":"bastiodon","speciesId":411,"dex":411,"form":"normal","generation":4,"types":["rock","steel"],"stats":{"hp":60,"attack":52,"defense":168,"special-attack":47,"special-defense":138,"speed":30},"abilities":[{"name":"sturdy","hidden":false},{"name":"soundproof","hidden":true}],"height":13,"weight":1495,"baseExp":173,"sprites":{"normal":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/411.png","shiny":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/shiny/411.png","icon":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/411.png"},"cry":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/cries/main/cries/pokemon/latest/411.ogg","genus":"Shield Pokémon","genusPt":"Pokémon de escudo","flavor":[{"version":"diamond","text":"Any frontal attack is repulsed. It is a docile Pokémon that feeds on grass and berries."},{"version":"pearl","text":"When attacked, they form a wall with their shieldlike faces to protect their young."},{"version":"platinum","text":"When they lined up side by side, no foe could break through. They shielded their young in that way."},{"version":"heartgold","text":"When attacked, they form a wall. Their rock-hard faces serve to protect them from the attacks."},{"version":"sun","text":"While it can guard against any sort of attack from the front, it is left without recourse when attacked from behind."},{"version":"moon","text":"It lived in the same environments as Rampardos. Their fossils have been found together— seemingly from after they’d fought to the finish."},{"version":"ultra-sun","text":"The bones of its face are huge and hard, so they were mistaken for its spine until after this Pokémon was successfully restored."},{"version":"ultra-moon","text":"This Pokémon is from roughly 100 million years ago. Its terrifyingly tough face is harder than steel."},{"version":"legends-arceus","text":"Its face is sturdy—as strong as diamond—a